{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes","id":1506833,"title":"For Fun - Dissonance-free Dragonriders and Other Fantasy Troupes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-29T02:39:05-07:00","id":1506833,"title":"For Fun - Dissonance-free Dragonriders and Other Fantasy Troupes","content":"The occasional bit of levity or absurdity can be a nice counterpoint to the more monstrous aspect of Mages. To that end...<br /> <br /> What options does a Mage have for acquiring fantasy mounts? Like, a dragon, a pegasus, a giant tortoise with a palinquin, etc. <u>Transform Life</u> or <u>Create Lif</u>e are subject to Dissonance*, as is <u>Shapechange</u>, and you can't defy physics anyway without the easily-eroded <u>Levitation</u>. <br /> A <u><i>Familiar</i></u> -spirits being the most likely, though Goetia could do in a pinch with some assistance- could manifest into a rideable state. Just don't use a spell-created entity.<br /> <br /> Maybe a <i>Fae Mount</i>? Not sure if a Mage is eligible, but as long as you can feed it glamour and it has the Actormask perk, you can bring all kinds of creatures into the world. 'Course, the Mask eliminates some of the awe of &quot;goddammit dragon rider&quot;.<br /> <br /> I dont know the other lines well, so anyone have options I missed?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*For the first generation, at any rate, with the Reach effect.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T05:57:52-07:00","id":1506843,"title":"","content":"I'd do the Reading Rainbow thing. Go into a bookstore, find the highest-rated spirit of <i>Fiction</i> or whatever, and see what it wants to let me ride Drogon to do my errands.<br /> <br /> The rivers of the Underworld supposedly have dinosaurs in them if you are feeling aquatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T06:14:23-07:00","id":1506844,"title":"","content":"Introduce enough children to the Never Ending Story that you can get them to make spirits of Falcor, then use Spirit / whatever to empower it until it's a full freaking dragon spirit, bring down the gauntlet to let it cross over and ride a Luck Dragon spirit all around town?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T06:52:45-07:00","id":1506848,"title":"","content":"Placing the subjects of <i>Transform Life</i> in an area with <i>Temporal Pocket</i> combined with <i>Veil of Moments</i> means that you can iterate through generations quickly, and without the risk that comes with altering their reproductive speed.<br /> <br /> Building on what ShadowCatX mentioned, with a Making of Mind you could make your idea of a luck dragon into a memetic feeling, that way it propagates well and the feelings people use to generate the spirit can be precisely tailored to your specifications. The meme is temporary, but what it generates is independent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T11:42:10-07:00","id":1506861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506848#post1506848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Placing the subjects of <i>Transform Life</i> in an area with <i>Temporal Pocket</i> combined with <i>Veil of Moments</i> means that you can iterate through generations quickly, and without the risk that comes with altering their reproductive speed.<br /> <br /> Building on what ShadowCatX mentioned, with a Making of Mind you could make your idea of a luck dragon into a memetic feeling, that way it propagates well and the feelings people use to generate the spirit can be precisely tailored to your specifications. The meme is temporary, but what it generates is independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking to Temporal pocket.<br /> <br /> If it is an area of effect, and you want your Life Creation inside (are you in there too?) Can you possess the creation, and then cast Temporal Pocket on yourself while your body is outside the pocket.<br /> <br /> Would you be able to live an effective lifetime in the Temporal pocket while your body doesn't age at all outside the pocket?<br /> <br /> That aside, to the OPs question, you can find Stigmatics and Cryptids who have been exposed to God-Machine infrastructure.<br /> <br /> I would have to read more about the details, but I'm sure Demon goes into it somewhere.<br /> <br /> If you wanted something more mundane, vampires can ghoul animals, hell hounds or similar, maybe a ghouled horse or elephant...<br /> <br /> If you can convince a Werewolf to give you a piggy back, then they seem likely to he strong enough to do so (not sure what else they have, probably spirits).<br /> <br /> Can the Created bring fantastical animals to life?<br /> <br /> Mage has the existence of Emanation Realms. Lots of creatures might be found in one, depending on what suits your setting, whether they would be immune to dissonance or not is unclear to my mind.<br /> <br /> I don't know Mummy or Deviant all that well, and i suspect Hunters don't get to have so much fun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T13:39:41-07:00","id":1506870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506861#post1506861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking to Temporal pocket.<br /> <br /> If it is an area of effect, and you want your Life Creation inside (are you in there too?) Can you possess the creation, and then cast Temporal Pocket on yourself while your body is outside the pocket.<br /> <br /> Would you be able to live an effective lifetime in the Temporal pocket while your body doesn't age at all outside the pocket?<br /> <br /> That aside, to the OPs question, you can find Stigmatics and Cryptids who have been exposed to God-Machine infrastructure.<br /> <br /> I would have to read more about the details, but I'm sure Demon goes into it somewhere.<br /> <br /> If you wanted something more mundane, vampires can ghoul animals, hell hounds or similar, maybe a ghouled horse or elephant...<br /> <br /> If you can convince a Werewolf to give you a piggy back, then they seem likely to he strong enough to do so (not sure what else they have, probably spirits).<br /> <br /> Can the Created bring fantastical animals to life?<br /> <br /> Mage has the existence of Emanation Realms. Lots of creatures might be found in one, depending on what suits your setting, whether they would be immune to dissonance or not is unclear to my mind.<br /> <br /> I don't know Mummy or Deviant all that well, and i suspect Hunters don't get to have so much fun...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you are using <i>Possession</i>, then that means you probably have a good grasp of Mind. So lets say you have both specialists available, the you can use <i>Gain Skill</i> to be able to build a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\">mechanized juggernaut</a> that you can possess. What's more, no human pilot means no need for a cockpit or any of those limiting safety features, probably giving a few more points for modifications. Without additional spellwork, the caster will have to deal with ammo and the power cell running out. But it will make quite an impression, and it won't be Dissonanced away, since having a piece of top secret tech be piloted remotely is not that far fetched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T17:01:39-07:00","id":1506888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506870#post1506870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if you are using <i>Possession</i>, then that means you probably have a good grasp of Mind. So lets say you have both specialists available, the you can use <i>Gain Skill</i> to be able to build a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\">mechanized juggernaut</a> that you can possess. What's more, no human pilot means no need for a cockpit or any of those limiting safety features, probably giving a few more points for modifications. Without additional spellwork, the caster will have to deal with ammo and the power cell running out. But it will make quite an impression, and it won't be Dissonanced away, since having a piece of top secret tech be piloted remotely is not that far fetched.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Possession work on automatons? I can see a workaround by using <u>Golem</u> with the Mind expansion and applying <u>Telepathy</u> to it - you give orders over the link, and make the base personality basically your own but subservient to you. Needs a pretty heavy Arcana investment, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T17:17:23-07:00","id":1506892,"title":"","content":"I believe so, having the object be articulated only gives it a greater range of motion. One way I like to visualize it is like the Gamecube shooter <i>Geist</i>, which is a good example of creative ways a Mastigos could use <i>Psychic Projection</i> and <i>Posssession</i> in problemsolving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T23:46:47-07:00","id":1506930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506888#post1506888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Possession work on automatons? I can see a workaround by using <u>Golem</u> with the Mind expansion and applying <u>Telepathy</u> to it - you give orders over the link, and make the base personality basically your own but subservient to you. Needs a pretty heavy Arcana investment, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can possess an inanimate objects, feel what it is like to *be* a car for a while. But unless it is a self-driving car you'll have trouble actually doing anything.<br /> <br /> You don't need the conjunctional Mind with a Golem to give it a Mind, i think you can just possess it (imagine someone else's Golem being taken over...) And take control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T00:46:56-07:00","id":1506932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506930#post1506930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need the conjunctional Mind with a Golem to give it a Mind, i think you can just possess it (imagine someone else's Golem being taken over...) And take control.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was more to create an autonomous entity that you nominally control, without having to abandon your own body, but yes, if <u>Possession</u> can indeed affect objects you can get up to some shenanigans. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T03:39:11-07:00","id":1506938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506932#post1506932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was more to create an autonomous entity that you nominally control, without having to abandon your own body, but yes, if <u>Possession</u> can indeed affect objects you can get up to some shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think without Mastery of Mind, you could take a part of your personality, a summoned goetia from your Oneiros, and stuff that in...<br /> <br /> But the basic Golem/Eidolon/Zombie spells all grant the retainer merit and allows the retainer follow basic commands.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T05:21:02-07:00","id":1506941,"title":"","content":"<i>Possession </i>allows the being to control the object as if it was being operated by a person. Which is why ghosts could have possessed a six shift car and used it to get revenge. The more high tech, the easier to control the vessel.<br /> <br /> This is also why its so easy to confuse a strong Mastigos with a Moros, they can simply make a zombie army by making goetia take over a corpse. They are fully articulated, so they make effective vessels that do not require preparation work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T10:22:42-07:00","id":1506959,"title":"","content":"And i think it is Patterning rather than weaving to turn a memory into a Goetia.<br /> <br /> It is probably not dissonance free, to have goetia possess corpses - or arguably you give the goetia the possession manifestation (using Death or Spirit*) and it is now using a manifestation which is not Supernal?<br /> <br /> *The only manifestation which Mind should actually have access to is possession imo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T10:56:40-07:00","id":1506961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1506843#post1506843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd do the Reading Rainbow thing. Go into a bookstore, find the highest-rated spirit of <i>Fiction</i> or whatever, and see what it wants to let me ride Drogon to do my errands.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how Influences work; an Influence of &quot;Create Fiction&quot; is going to bring a work of fiction into existence, not make a thing that was fictional become real.<br /> <br /> Also it's typically going to belong to a spirit of rank 4 or 5, which is not going to be encountered casually and be a bit perilous to deal with. The highest rated spirit you're likely to find in any random bookstore you go into is 2, and even if Influence: Fiction could conjure fictional things into existence, it's not going to do that at the &quot;manipulate&quot; level.<br /> <br /> I think the Awakened will be well suited to discovering creatures that might be made amenable to riding with Life or Mind magic that already exist naturally in the Fallen World, some of which might be regarded as Cryptids and some that might have certain other quirks. I think it can help to get a trail to pick up for such things in folklore and urban legend about strange beings off the edge of the map, but perhaps the most immediate thing that can be done is calling upon those entities that bestow divined knowledge; a Supernal Being aligned with the Life Arcanum (especially an Atavism of the Primal Wilds) or visiting Stag or Snake of the Aeons might be used to acquire a starting point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T21:19:08-07:00","id":1507017,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could ask an appropriate Beast nicely? Surely someone has a dragon as a Horror and is willing to humor you.<br /> <br /> As for Deviant, well manticores are a thing. Give a big lizard the right Variations, and you will end up with something resembling a dragon. As far as I'm aware, anyone can have a manticore pet, given the right connections and/or knowledge. With 5 dots of Manticore Companion, you could get a Komodo Dragon with Flight 3, Gigantic 3, and Lash (Ranged, Lethal) for a pretty good approximation. One could drop one of any of those to push the others up to 4 if you wanted a faster, bigger, or deadlier dragon.<br /> <br /> I don't know Promethean's enemies as well, maybe some Centimani grabbed some Ordo Dracul symbolism, and turned themselves into Alchemy Powered Dragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-31-2023, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:22:08-07:00","id":1507033,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s try finding a way to get a dragon with all the Arcana.<br /> <br /> <b>Death</b>: Get a ghost, then use your own magic or another ghost\u2019s Moliate Numen to get a dragon shape. Or try to catch a draconic Chthonian.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate</b>: Luck yourself into coming across a dragon. Which is likely a fairy, given how Fate interacts with them extensively.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces</b>: If you have Prime too, Imbue some fire and flight magic into a monitor lizard or an alligator.<br /> Alternatively, be always ready to throw fireballs whenever your pet reptile \u2018roars\u2019. For the people who object, throw more fireballs.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Fleshcraft and breed your own dragons!<br /> <br /> <b>Matter</b>: Jury-rig yourself a transforming dragon mecha from flamethrowers and drones.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind</b>: Summon a Goetia.<br /> Alternatively, befriend a Beast with a draconic Horror, and either ask him for a piggyback or adopt a Horrorspawn from him.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlternatively, conjure a hallucination of a dragon.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime</b>: See the above bit about Imbuement. Alternatively, throw enough magic to track down Verges where draconic Cryptids may live.<br /> <br /> <b>Space</b>: As scouting for Verges above, but this time look for interstices that contain \u2018real\u2019 dragons.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b>: Summon a spirit. Surely some specimens among the courts of fire, waters, earth, and gold look like dragons.<br /> <br /> <b>Time</b>: Wow this is hard. No clue myself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:43:30-07:00","id":1507037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507033#post1507033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Forces</b>: If you have Prime too, Imbue some fire and flight magic into a monitor lizard or an alligator.<br /> Alternatively, be always ready to throw fireballs whenever your pet reptile \u2018roars\u2019. For the people who object, throw more fireballs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the fireball spell be subject to Dissonance if peope go in expecting a dragon to breath fire? Flight would probably work fine as long as it has wings and noolbody thinks too hard about the aerodynamics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Time</b>: Wow this is hard. No clue myself! </div> </div> </div>Slen Tiid Vo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:53:13-07:00","id":1507040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507037#post1507037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the fireball spell be subject to Dissonance if peope go in expecting a dragon to breath fire? Flight would probably work fine as long as it has wings and noolbody thinks too hard about the aerodynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Imbued version?<br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026 belief doesn\u2019t affect the Sleeping Curse, so expectation shouldn\u2019t either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Slen Tiid Vo! </div> </div> </div>Is that even possible with Awakened magic, though? Archmastery, OTOH\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T02:01:23-07:00","id":1507041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507040#post1507040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that even possible with Awakened magic, though? Archmastery, OTOH\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Deny the Reaper</u> can resurrect the dead, so bringing dinosaurs to life with Death (and then possibly modifying them with <u>Transform Life</u>) would be close.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T05:37:47-07:00","id":1507052,"title":"","content":"Temporal Summon an actual Dragon(use various predictive powers to find the required Temporal sympathy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T12:03:51-07:00","id":1507064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507041#post1507041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Deny the Reaper</u> can resurrect the dead, so bringing dinosaurs to life with Death (and then possibly modifying them with <u>Transform Life</u>) would be close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deny the Reaper works on the <i>recently</i> dead.<br /> <br /> Temporal Summoning doesn't work on the dead at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:06:02-07:00","id":1507070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507052#post1507052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporal Summon an actual Dragon(use various predictive powers to find the required Temporal sympathy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons were the patrons of Atlantis, they were erased when it was and all that remains are their bones (which require ruins of the Time Before to function). Its likely trying would trip some kind of archmage level safeguard, since dragons were archmasters long before humans. Having them return could be terrifying even to Ascended beings.<br /> <br /> Creating dragons with Time is rough, the best I got is to use <i>Rewrite History</i> to make the mage into a genius biologist with ample Resources. Then use <i>Converging Potentiality</i> to make them become a one man research team, break down all the things needed to genetically engineer a dragon and then use <i>Blink of an Eye</i> to complete each subproject in seconds.<br /> <br /> Would it be convoluted ? Yes. But it does have the potential for results that cannot be dispelled, or for scientific abominations rampaging through the city. <br /> <br /> In theory, if the mage powers through with <i>Veil of Moments</i>, by the end of the third day they probably figured out useful applications of the side projects, placing them decades ahead of modern medicine.<br /> <br /> <i>Temporal Summoning</i> and <i>Deny The Reaper </i>could bring the dinosaurs back, the former placing the corpse within range for the effect of the latter.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:26:34-07:00","id":1507073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1507070#post1507070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragons were the patrons of Atlantis, they were erased when it was and all that remains are their bones (which require ruins of the Time Before to function). Its likely trying would trip some kind of archmage level safeguard, since dragons were archmasters long before humans. Having them return could be terrifying even to Ascended beings.<br /> <br /> &lt;Snip&gt;<br /> <br /> <i>Temporal Summoning</i> and <i>Deny The Reaper </i>could bring the dinosaurs back, the former placing the corpse within range for the effect of the latter.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, are you suggesting you can't go to the ruins of the time before, find a Dragon bone, and then Temporal Summon/deny the reaper? Ideally Deny the Reaper just needs lots of reach, right? No the spell says recently dead... Presumably you can cast deny the reaper and give the thing a soul... If it was Archmaster level Awakened or Ascended... Yeah that would be bad. But if it has a normal human soul attached, i don't know how it would access the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:41:19-07:00","id":1508243,"title":"","content":"There is a dragon in the Ascension-book; imagine a dragon-mount like Smaug;<i> &quot;Really; you're doing to ride me? Am I your palfrey?&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T10:32:56-07:00","id":1508282,"title":"","content":"Ok, since Temporal summoning seems to be unfairly limited (though it is only Weaving) i have a seperate plan.<br /> <br /> Temporal pocket, combined with natural evolutionary pressure (or possibly a fate spell to end when a Dragon has evolved ...) You create an accelerated environment where breeding pairs of some Dragon like entity exist, along with something to make them giant, fire breathing and winged... So island gigantism, some sort of predator prey relationship where the evolutionary arms race requires fire breathing... (And presumably means you have also selected for a fire proof creature... Unless it is sexual selection between Dragons which means they are likely also the fire proof ones...) And something to make flight an advantage... That bit may be hard.<br /> <br /> Conditional duration to make the bubble last a million year (instead of indefinite) so you can check in on your experiment... Or stay inside and Temporal stutter yourself a hundred thousand years into the future at a time (and hope the pocket doesn't end prematurely leaving you stuttering into the distant future...).<br /> <br /> Add judicious use of Prophecy to figure out the best steps to take at each stage, and you have a plan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T10:58:06-07:00","id":1508284,"title":"","content":"In Second Edition, the Diamond Orders don't necessarily literally believe that the ancient progenitors of magic were something that could be described as dragons any more than they think the Awakened City was some kind of ocean spire.<br /> <br /> The dragon fixation is a holdover from when the Tremere were in the sect.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Temporal Pocket doesn't create accelerate time within a space, it causes a subject to experience the flow of time detached from everything else.<br /> <br /> And ends the moment they consume things.<br /> <br /> You'd end that spell and find a very fine pile of dust.<br /> <br /> Although if you cast it over an area, you're far more likely to have the ending condition of &quot;the animal walks out of it in search of food&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, evolution is not magic, accumulated traits need to be within things like biochemical possibilities, possible to reconcile with existing morphology, and basic physics. You can't evolution your way into something being able to defy gravity (birds can fly with the benefit of being incredibly light).<br /> <br /> &quot;Select for fire proof features&quot;; fire's effect on tissue is a function of what temperatures in excess of several hundred degrees does to protein structures, you cannot evolve into something resistant to that any more than you can evolve into a rock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T01:47:05-07:00","id":1508336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1508284#post1508284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Second Edition, the Diamond Orders don't necessarily literally believe that the ancient progenitors of magic were something that could be described as dragons any more than they think the Awakened City was some kind of ocean spire.<br /> <br /> The dragon fixation is a holdover from when the Tremere were in the sect.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Temporal Pocket doesn't create accelerate time within a space, it causes a subject to experience the flow of time detached from everything else.<br /> <br /> And ends the moment they consume things.<br /> <br /> You'd end that spell and find a very fine pile of dust.<br /> <br /> Although if you cast it over an area, you're far more likely to have the ending condition of &quot;the animal walks out of it in search of food&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, evolution is not magic, accumulated traits need to be within things like biochemical possibilities, possible to reconcile with existing morphology, and basic physics. You can't evolution your way into something being able to defy gravity (birds can fly with the benefit of being incredibly light).<br /> <br /> &quot;Select for fire proof features&quot;; fire's effect on tissue is a function of what temperatures in excess of several hundred degrees does to protein structures, you cannot evolve into something resistant to that any more than you can evolve into a rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this plan has nothing to do with the Tremere, as it is looking for future Dragons...<br /> <br /> In reverse order, you can entirely evolve something equivalent to a rigid aerofoam layer which is a very good insulator and takes only a tiny amount of mass (protiens) to produce.<br /> <br /> Birds tend to evolve flight, as have bats, flying fish, many insects, and pterasaurs.<br /> <br /> Lastly, yes, this requires an AoE spells, ideally you do it somewhere with its own source of food, (which is naturally regenerating) and where sleepers will not accidentally wander (though with all the effects happening instantly there is not time for them to wander in).<br /> <br /> A pocket dimension (space mastery) would be ideal.<br /> <br /> Using prophecy to find the right steps to take to get the correct evolutionary pressures is vital, but since you have effectively infinite time... Your only real limit is the scale of the AoE and how to keep the creatures you evolve from wandering off (Pocket Dimension looking more attractive on that matter...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T02:52:46-07:00","id":1508346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1508336#post1508336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, this plan has nothing to do with the Tremere, as it is looking for future Dragons...</div> </div> </div> </div>People are here talking about the idea of getting Atlantean dragons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reverse order, you can entirely evolve something equivalent to a rigid aerofoam layer which is a very good insulator and takes only a tiny amount of mass (protiens) to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insulation is so not fire-proofing.<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way; proteins start to break down in the presence of temperatures around 44 degrees Celsius. That's why people can be burned by the kind of temperatures you can get from a shower. <br /> <br /> The weakest flames possible burn in excess of 500 degrees. Visible orange flames are more like 1100.<br /> <br /> There is no form of organic life that does not flake away in contact with fire. It is literally impossible. You cannot make a protective layer out of a substance that will fall apart in contact with what you're looking to be protected from.<br /> <br /> You can't evolve into it, you can't even use magic to bestow it as a hereditary trait because those still need to be things some existing form of life has. Give something the capabilities of an extremophile bacterium and they'll survive being steamed in an autoclave, which is still ten times less hot than fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birds tend to evolve flight, as have bats, flying fish, many insects, and pterasaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason most of those are too small for a human to ride (and the biggest pterosaur was probably not very strong).<br /> <br /> It's a simple question of weight ratios. A five ounce bird can not carry a one pound coconut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, yes, this requires an AoE spells, ideally you do it somewhere with its own source of food, (which is naturally regenerating)</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of food is that?<br /> <br /> Not that it matters much when it specifically says the spell breaks if a subject consumes something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T04:55:17-07:00","id":1508352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506833-for-fun-dissonance-free-dragonriders-and-other-fantasy-troupes?p=1508346#post1508346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of food is that?<br /> <br /> Not that it matters much when it specifically says the spell breaks if a subject consumes something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that is consume anything which is not in the Temporal pocket. Anything inside the AoE should be consumable as normal. <br /> <br /> If it included a Hallow, there would he some question as to whether it would refill at the rate of subjective time inside the bubble or at the rate time flows outside of the bubble.<br /> <br /> If time masters could just cast Temporal Pocket on any hallow they come across and have it block up with Tass forming around it every day, that might be a little game breaky.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}